### **Media Queries in CSS**  
Media queries in CSS allow you to apply different styles based on the screen size, resolution, or device type. They are useful for making websites responsive.

### **Basic Syntax**
```css
@media (condition) {
  /* CSS rules here */
}
```

### **Common Examples**

#### **1. Changing Styles Based on Screen Width**
```css
/* Styles for screens wider than 600px */
@media (min-width: 600px) {
  body {
    background-color: lightblue;
  }
}

/* Styles for screens smaller than 600px */
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  body {
    background-color: pink;
  }
}
```

#### **2. Responsive Layout for Different Devices**
```css
/* For tablets */
@media (min-width: 600px) and (max-width: 1024px) {
  body {
    font-size: 18px;
  }
}

/* For desktop screens */
@media (min-width: 1025px) {
  body {
    font-size: 20px;
  }
}
```

#### **3. Hiding an Element on Small Screens**
```css
@media (max-width: 500px) {
  .sidebar {
    display: none;
  }
}
```

#### **4. Media Query for Dark Mode**
```css
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  body {
    background-color: black;
    color: white;
  }
}
```

### **Key Media Features**
| Media Feature | Description |
|--------------|------------|
| `min-width` | Applies styles when the screen is at least a certain width |
| `max-width` | Applies styles when the screen is at most a certain width |
| `min-height` | Applies styles based on screen height |
| `max-height` | Applies styles based on screen height |
| `orientation: portrait` | Applies styles when the device is in portrait mode |
| `orientation: landscape` | Applies styles when the device is in landscape mode |
| `prefers-color-scheme: dark` | Detects if the user prefers dark mode |

